From a15f38adcc6dbb6b3e7b2c049c601f037c6153cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: a video whose stream says nothing of HDR
 is what its decoded picture is, HLG or HDR10

The format of the input of the player information (HadesSourceFormatVar)
was VideoPlayer.HdrType, the demuxer's: the transfer function that the
container or the stream says when it opens. A stream that says none
there, as an add-on's stream of YouTube in HLG may, was named SDR, while
its decoded pictures are HLG (ARIB STD-B67) and the display was sent HLG
for them (SetHDR() goes by the picture). The badge of the overview
(hades.sum.vbadge), its sentence and heading, the labels named as in the
CoreELEC builds and the notice of the playback mode all read
hades.src.hdrtype, which said the same.

hades.src.hdrtype now says what the decoded picture is where the stream
says nothing of HDR and has no Dolby Vision record: HLG for ARIB
STD-B67, HDR10 for PQ (HDR10+ while its frames carry that metadata)
(PLAYERINFO::SourceHdrType()). What a stream says is never changed.
Estuary's format of the input, and the pages of Hades for other skins
made again from it (tools/hades-playerinfo), read it where
VideoPlayer.HdrType is empty. VideoPlayer.HdrType itself stays the
stream's, as Kodi has it, for skins, add-ons and JSON-RPC.

The transfer function comes from what the video says of itself
(CWinSystemGbm::SourceColour, the line of colour of the player
information), which SetHDR() notes from the picture it is given. For an
HDR10 or HLG picture mapped to SDR, or adapted to the display, the
renderer gives it the picture made for the output: the line of colour
said BT.709 for an HLG film on an SDR display, and the mastering display
of the film was the peak told to the display. CLinuxRendererGLES now
tells the picture of the video after SetHDR() in that case
(NoteSourceColour()).

The idea comes from CroqueMr's report of HLG input
(libreelec-x86-DV, preview/rc4-update3, 23b37d0c7a, "Correct HLG input
reporting"); found by vertox with YouTube in HLG. Written for this tree,
for PQ as well, and for every place that names the format.
